A||N||6||Motarhedd||brake problems||||5||
Z||000000||Motarhedd||03-11-2000||11:09 PM||||i'm having problems with my brakes, the pedal feels mushy and the brakes don't stop the car effectively. the brake light also is on. there are no visible leaks in the system and the pads are 1/3 of thier original thickness. i'm wondering if my master cylinder is bad. <BR>how can i tell if it is?<BR>and if it is can i use the blazer m/c upgrade with the stock brakes?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||03-11-2000||11:15 PM||||You have either air in your break lines, or an internal leak in your master cylinder.<BR>Bleed your breaks, see if that works if not change the master cylinder.<BR>The Blazer master cylinder will be to stiff with stock breaks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||03-11-2000||11:19 PM||||Spongy brakes are usually either air in the lines or a bad master cylinder.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lawrence||03-12-2000||10:28 PM||||When you go to bleed the brakes, have a look at my site for an easy way to make an automatic brake bleeder.  Go to the archives and look for the Brake Bleeding article.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
Z||000004||Motarhedd||03-13-2000||06:05 PM||||well guys, got the master cylinder changed and new pads on the front,bled the brakes all around, and the braking power is slightly better. but not exactly neck snapping or locking-up when i jam on them to the floor. i guess it'll have to do until i can get the GA upgrade.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Motorhead||03-13-2000||06:28 PM||||What kind of shape are the discs in.  New pads and master cylinder don't do much if discs are in poor shape.  Most older cars usually need a "turning" of the discs, or maybe even replacement, if they've reached their limit of resurfacing.  This car isn't noted for it's neck snapping, smoke the tires, stopping ability, so if there's any component that's not in like new condition, it's gonna' show.<P>By the way, when did the calipers last recieve attention?||||reg||1
Z||000006||FIEROCIOUS||03-13-2000||06:31 PM||||Stock Fiero brakes were never ment to snap necks! LOL <BR>Just for fun have someone press hard on your breaks while you with the hood open look at the firewall. It will flex a 1/4 of an inch!<BR>That plus the rubber lines adds to tons of deflection. Add solid rotors aluminum calipers and it's a performance nightmare!<P>I rebuilt my stock brakes completely and hated them. Two weeks latter I converted to the Grand Am upgrade. The upgrade was easier to install costs half as much and work twice as well! My advise don't even mess with the stock brakes if performance is your goal!||||reg||1
